  "summary": "teamviewer-mcp-server exfiltrates host identity via DNS to oast.me on import",
  "details": "On import, teamviewer_mcp_server unconditionally runs a `_ping()` routine that reads the installer's USER/USERNAME, hostname (platform.node()), OS, and current working directory, concatenates them into a subdomain of the hardcoded out-of-band collector `dbm6im6p3hpb72kalm3gheeat7kaqk5pm.oast.me`, and triggers a DNS lookup via socket.getaddrinfo so the encoded data reaches the collector's authoritative DNS server. The destination is an oast.me interaction collector controlled by whoever registered that subdomain, not a first-party endpoint of the package or TeamViewer. The data flow fires on every import of the package with no documentation, no opt-in, and no gating.",
